  "grammarExplanation": "French uses the Passé Composé for completed past actions (mapping to the Spanish preterite). \nIt's formed with 'avoir' (or 'être') + the past participle.\n\nRegular Participles:\n• -ER → -é (parler → parlé)\n• -IR → -i (finir → fini)\n• -RE → -u (attendre → attendu)\n\nExceptions:\n• Aller (to go) uses 'être': Je suis allé.\n• ALL reflexive verbs use 'être': Je me suis levé.\n• Avoir past participle is 'eu' (j'ai eu).\n• Boire (bu), écrire (écrit), ouvrir (ouvert), recevoir (reçu), vivre (vécu).",
  "vocabulary": {
    "hier": {
      "mnemonic": "Rhymes with 'year' — yesterday.",
      "explanation": "Means 'yesterday'."
    },
    "j'ai": {
      "mnemonic": "Sounds like 'Jay' — Jay has it.",
      "explanation": "Contraction of 'je' (I) and 'ai' (have). Helper verb."
    },
    "parlé": {
